---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SocialSecurityLab from "../../components/SocialSecurityLab.tsx";
import NextTool from "../../components/NextTool.astro";
import Sources from "../../components/Sources.astro";
import "../../styles/simtool.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="When to Claim Social Security"
  description="The core trade-off in claiming Social Security: bigger checks later versus more checks sooner. See delayed-retirement credits, the breakeven age, and longevity risk."
>
  <section class="container wl-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Interactive Tool</p>
    <h1>When should you claim Social Security?</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      You can start Social Security anytime from 62 to 70, and the choice is
      worth tens of thousands of dollars. This optimizer weighs every age by how
      likely you are to <em>live to collect it</em> — then lets you personalize
      the two levers that actually move the answer: your <strong>health</strong>
      (how long you'll likely live) and your <strong>discount rate</strong>
      (including whether you'd use the money to pay down debt).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-host">
    <SocialSecurityLab client:load />
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-explainer">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>How the optimizer thinks</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Bigger checks vs. more of them.</strong> Claiming at 62 shrinks
          your check to ~70% of the full amount but starts eight years sooner;
          waiting to 70 lifts it to ~124% via delayed-retirement credits. The
          breakeven for waiting is usually around age 80–81.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Survival-weighting.</strong> Rather than pick a single "live
          until" age, we weight each future check by your probability of being
          alive to cash it, using the SSA life table — then present-value the
          whole stream. The tallest bar is the age that maximizes it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The health premium.</strong> Not smoking and staying active
          meaningfully shift your survival curve — which changes both your
          expected lifetime benefits and the optimal claim age. Longevity is a
          return no portfolio guarantees, and it's badly under-appreciated.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Debt is a discount rate.</strong> Using early benefits to retire
          a 6% mortgage <em>is</em> a 6% return. So carrying costly debt raises
          your effective discount rate and tilts the answer toward claiming
          earlier — which the discount-rate slider lets you model directly.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        A single-earner teaching model: it leaves out spousal and survivor
        benefits, taxes, the earnings test, and your exact record. For an actual,
        personalized filing strategy, use the free, open-source
        <a href="https://opensocialsecurity.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open Social Security</a>
        by Mike Piper — the reference this tool is modeled on and cross-checked
        against. Educational only, not advice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Sources tool="social-security" />

  <NextTool current="/tools/social-security" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wl-intro {
    padding-block: var(--space-lg) var(--space-md);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .wl-explainer {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }
</style>

<style is:global>
  .ss-compare {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.3rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
  }
  .ss-compare-item {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.1rem;
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 0.35rem 0.3rem;
    border: var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--color-bg);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }
  .ss-compare-item.active {
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
    background: var(--color-accent-soft);
  }
  .ss-compare-age {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
  .ss-compare-amt {
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    white-space: nowrap;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }
  .ss-legend {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem 0.9rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .ss-legend span {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }
  .ss-key {
    width: 1.1rem;
    height: 0;
    flex: none;
    border-top-width: 3px;
    border-top-style: solid;
  }
  .ss-key--c1 {
    border-top-color: var(--pl-c1);
  }
  .ss-key--c2 {
    border-top-color: var(--pl-c2);
  }
  .ss-key--c3 {
    border-top-color: var(--pl-c3);
  }
  .ss-key--sel {
    border-top-color: var(--color-accent);
    border-top-width: 4px;
  }
  .ss-headline {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--color-accent-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-accent);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }
  .ss-headline-label {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .ss-headline-value {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .ss-headline-sub {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .ss-stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
  }
  .ss-stats > div {
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .ss-stats dt {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }
  .ss-stats dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .ss-oss h3 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }
  .ss-oss p {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .ss-oss-link {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-0);
  }
  .ss-credit {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    border: var(--border);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--space-sm);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .ss-credit a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .ss-seg-field {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }
  .ss-seg-label {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .ss-seg {
    display: flex;
    gap: 4px;
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 4px;
  }
  .ss-seg button {
    flex: 1;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.3rem;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 7px;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    cursor: pointer;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .ss-seg button.active {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    color: var(--color-accent);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }
  .ss-health h3 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }
  .ss-health p {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
</style>
